e and even if it's a little  scary or intimidating just dive right in  recently I took a bet on myself I quit  my day job I moved 30 miles north and I  got a full-time job at a bakery it was a  it was scary because it wanted something  new you know I'm I'm not a bread  professional I'm going into a space  where people have been working in bread  for years and and they really know what  they're doing so it's it's a little it's  a little intimidating but I knew if I  didn't if I didn't go take this bakery  job that I would be staying in a day job  that was relatively easy comfortable fun  but I would always have in the back of  my head that I didn't go chase my dreams  and I feel like one day I look back when  I was 40 or 50 or 70 or 80 and I'll say  why didn't I go take that chance when I  had it when when it was like right there  in front of me yeah I don't want that  moment to come I want I want to say that  I want to be able to say in five years  when I have this bakery space that I'm  that I'm hoping to have one day that I  did go follow my dreams and I think this  is the first step that I'm taking  happiness looks like being able to share  the bread that I make with other people  watching those people share what they  know with others my ultimate sourdough  dream is to share my love of bread with  other people through a small intimate  baking space where I can make bread and  give it to people and I can also teach  people how to make their own bread  I think that's what some what's the most  thrilling about sourdough to me is that  every time I bake bread and make the  dough it's different and I'm still  enthralled by it it kind of feels like  it kind of feels like following in love  because you're like obsessed with it  you're thinking about it all the time  and and you want to learn more about it  and it doesn't stop it hasn't stopped  things it's only been a couple of years  but I imagine it's not gonna stop  chasing my dreams like feels like I got  on a train that is going really fast and  it's a little scary but I'm like hanging  on for dear life and I'm really excited  for where it's gonna take me I had been  held back by thinking oh like you know I  can't do that I'm I'm young I don't you  know I don't have a lot of money or I I  don't have the resources to do that but  you can you can make the business that  you want to make if you have the skills  to do it and the creativity and also the  passion because it's a lot of hard work  so seeing other people chase their  dreams and makes make their passions a  reality has allowed me to feel like I  can do that too my name is Marissa Bui  my passion is sourdough bread baking and  I'm following my food dreams oh yes  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

